course: dictionary
lesson: 14432
title: Owned: who something belongs to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Owned is the past form of own. It means something was yours before, or belonged to someone. «Sam owned a red bike last year.» Sam might not have that bike now, but last year it was his.
explain: Owned with by tells you who something belongs to. «The shop is owned by my uncle.» The word after by is the person who has the shop. Ask yourself: who has it?
explain: Owned can join another word to make a describing word. «We ate at a family-owned café.» The café belongs to one family. The hyphen joins family and owned so they work together as one describing word.
fact: Owned is the past form of own: own, owns, owned, owning.
fact: «Owned» means belonged to someone, or was yours before.
fact: Owned by tells you who something belongs to: «a bike owned by Priya».
fact: «Family-owned» means owned by a family, like «a family-owned farm».
fact: In maths, owned can mean how much you had at the start: «Tom owned 10 marbles» means 10 was the starting amount.
exercise: «The bakery was owned by Mrs Okafor for twenty years.» Who owned the bakery? | The bakery was closed | *Mrs Okafor | Twenty years
exercise: «Lily owned a green scooter, but now it is her brother's.» What does owned mean here? | Lost on the way home | Painted green | Wanted to buy | *Belonged to Lily, in the past
exercise: «Tom owned 10 marbles. He gave 3 away.» How many marbles did Tom own at the start? | 13 | 7 | 3 | *10
test: «The castle was once owned by a king.» What does once show? | It happens every day | *It was a long time ago | It will happen next week
test: «The farm is family-owned.» What does family-owned mean? | Sold to a family next year | Painted by a family | *Belongs to a family
exam: Which sentence explains owned correctly? | Owned is only a word used in maths | *Owned is the past form of own, so it was yours before | Owned means something is lost forever | Owned means something is being built
